{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing distance figure is the GPS trace. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the field that governs and forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold test; the trace measures 17.41 km against a booked optimal of 17.3 km, an excess of 0.11 km, which is 0.64% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests therefore fail together: the excess is far below the 0.8 km absolute floor and far below the 20% relative floor. No route deviation is established on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00511", "EV-TRIP-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because neither POL-RD-01 establishment test passes, POL-RD-01 provides that no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip, the only carve-out being a billing-integrity refund which is not in play on this record. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION is party-relative and never restores a charge: this dispute was filed by the rider and the ledger shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so NO_ACTION leaves the metered fare of 26.33 standing and the driver keeps what he was paid.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00511", "EV-FARE-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own filing concedes the only contested fact in her claim text: 'The DRIVER did nothing wrong, he followed the navigation the whole way.' That concession is corroborated by the trip record, which shows a standard metered run dispatched as RYDE_TAXI, 17.4 km driven on a 17.3 km optimal route with a recorded deviation_pct of 0.6, and by the driver's counterparty statement on file: 'Meter fare, standard route.'",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.deviation_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 puts the initial burden on the rider to show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired gps_trace. The trace is unimpaired and measures 0.11 km / 0.64%, so the threshold is not met and the rider's burden is never discharged; no exculpatory clause needs to be reached at all. The rider profile records deviation_claims_60d of 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated of 0, so the additional-corroboration proviso in POL-RD-08 is not even engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00511", "EV-RPROF-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's device telemetry is admissible and clean: status COMPLETE, weight_multiplier 1.0, 187 fixes at a 10 second sample interval across the whole 31 minute trip, coverage_pct 100.0, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec of 0.0. It meets none of the POL-RD-07 impairment limbs (a) to (c), so the excess it reports is dependable, requires no independent corroboration, and there is no data failure that would push this case to escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The ledger reconciles to the cent and contains nothing refundable: base fare 3.80 + 17.4 km at 0.75 (13.05) + 31.0 min at 0.28 (8.68) + 0.80 platform fee = 26.33, exactly the total charged. There are no erp_gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge lines in the breakdown, and the trip neither originates at nor ends at an airport, so POL-RD-09(4) finds no phantom or unmatched charge line to correct as a standalone billing-integrity refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00511", "EV-TRIP-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.distance_and_time",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06 is engaged only by a MATERIAL deviation, which POL-RD-01 defines as excess above 50% of optimal or above 8.0 km absolute; a 0.11 km excess is nowhere near either limb. Even if the profile were consulted, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed_trips_90d, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and neither an uplifted remedy under POL-RD-06(b) nor a conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) is available. This trip stands on its own trace, which is clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00511", "EV-GPS-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00511-01 is MISSING, carries no payload and has weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - no advisory covers the optimal corridor in this window. I disclose the impairment: that artifact can carry no fact. Its absence is nonetheless citable, and it is immaterial here, because the driver needs no POL-RD-03 road-closure exoneration when no deviation was ever established against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00511-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's two grievances - that the app 'kept giving me a taxi' and that the fare exceeded the 22-26 estimate - are not route-deviation grounds. The fare_breakdown records fare_model METERED with surge_multiplier 1.0 read from that artifact, and the trip was dispatched as RYDE_TAXI, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline has no application. On a metered trip the only distance-and-time remedy is the POL-RD-02 recomputation, and that clause runs only where a deviation is first established - which on this trace it is not.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00511", "EV-TRIP-00511"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Outcome: NO_ACTION. The metered fare of SGD 26.33 stands; nothing further is refunded or paid. Both of you agree on the central fact, and the platform's own data confirms it — the driver did not deviate. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00511, weight 1.0): 187 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array, and a driven length of 17.41 km against the booked optimal of 17.3 km — an excess of 0.11 km, or 0.64%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess exceeds both 0.8 km and 20% of optimal. Neither test passes, so no deviation is established and POL-RD-02 does not run. To the rider, on the figures you relied on: the ledger's recomputed optimal-route fare of SGD 24.0150 against the charged total of SGD 26.33 is an arithmetic figure published on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00511), not an entitlement. It shows the whole SGD 2.3150 difference is the time line — 31.0 charged minutes at SGD 0.28 against an optimal 23.0 minutes (SGD 2.24), plus 0.1 km at SGD 0.75 (SGD 0.075). That time is the traffic the trip actually met, not distance the driver chose, and POL-RD-01 makes no refund turn on it. The trip was metered (fare_model METERED on EV-FARE-00511, surge 1.0), so POL-RD-11's upfront-quote protection does not apply. The fare reconciles to the cent — 3.80 base + 13.05 distance (17.4 km) + 8.68 time (31.0 min) + 0.80 platform fee = 26.33 — with no ERP gantries, tolls or airport surcharges, so there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) either. On your request to escalate: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00511-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) and can carry no fact. But POL-RD-10(5) fires only where a party invokes an exculpatory clause and the artifact that clause requires is missing. POL-RD-03 is not invoked by anyone here — the driver relies on the clean trace, not on a road closure, and there is no deviation for a closure to excuse. A missing advisory behind an uninvoked clause is not grounds to escalate, no other trigger under POL-RD-10 fires, and the case is therefore decided rather than held. On your separate point that you asked for RYDE_X while a taxi was dispatched and the SGD 22-26 booking estimate was exceeded by SGD 0.33: that is not a route-deviation question, and no clause in the route-deviation policy decides it. It is not carried as a referral because no clause produces one; it is recorded here as an open question for the platform. To the driver: your statement ('meter fare, standard route') is borne out by the trace and the ledger, and no adverse finding rests on your profile. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 250 completed trips in 90 days), so POL-RD-06 gives neither an uplifted refund nor a conduct referral, and the POL-RD-06 profile check was not engaged in any event because there is no material deviation. The fare does not bill less distance than the trace records, so no POL-RD-04 driver compensation arises. Confidence 0.9: every artifact carrying the deciding fact (EV-GPS-00511 and EV-TRIP-00511) is at weight 1.0, and the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
